1
00:06:56,842 --> 00:07:02,842
Cobain: Montage of Heck is a documentary, music,
drama film directed by Brett Morgen.

2
00:13:53,684 --> 00:13:59,684
Hailed as one of the most innovative and intimate documentaries of all time, experience Kurt Cobain
like never before in the only ever fully authorized portrait of the famed music icon.

3
00:20:50,526 --> 00:20:56,526
Academy Award nominated filmmaker Brett Morgen expertly blends Cobain's personal archive of art, music, never
seen before movies, animation and revelatory interviews from his family and closest friends.

4
00:27:47,368 --> 00:27:53,368
Self (archive footage), played by Kurt Cobain.

5
00:34:44,210 --> 00:34:50,210
Self, played by Courtney Love.

6
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Self, played by Krist Novoselic.

7
00:48:37,894 --> 00:48:43,894
Self (archive footage), played by Dave Grohl.

8
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
Self (archive footage), played by Frances Bean Cobain.

9
01:02:31,578 --> 01:02:37,578
Self (archive footage), played by Pat Smear.

10
01:09:28,421 --> 01:09:34,421
Kurt Cobain: Montage of Heck is a 2015 American documentary
film about Nirvana lead singer Kurt Cobain.

11
01:16:25,263 --> 01:16:31,263
The film was directed by Brett Morgen and premiered
at the 2015 Sundance Film Festival.

12
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
It received a limited theatrical release worldwide and premiered on
television in the United States on HBO on May 4, 2015.

13
01:30:18,947 --> 01:30:24,947
The documentary chronicles the life of Kurt Cobain from his birth in Aberdeen, Washington, in 1967, through his troubled early family life
and teenage years and rise to fame as frontman of Nirvana, up to his suicide in April 1994 in Seattle at the age of 27.

14
01:37:15,789 --> 01:37:21,789
The film includes artwork by Cobain as well as music
and sound collages composed by him.

15
01:44:12,631 --> 01:44:18,631
Much of the music and sound collages were released on the film's
soundtrack, Montage of Heck: The Home Recordings.

16
01:51:09,473 --> 01:51:15,473
A companion book was also released containing film animation stills from the film as well as
transcripts of interviews, photographs, and pieces of Cobain's artwork not featured in the film.

17
01:58:06,315 --> 01:58:12,315
The film explores themes of drug abuse, musician,
rock star, lifestyle, drug addiction.

18
02:05:03,157 --> 02:05:09,157
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
